# CI & SonarCloud Setup Guide — {{ model.manifest.service_name }}

## Overview

This guide documents CI and SonarCloud setup for an Angular/Nx workspace. Follow this top-to-bottom on any new repo for a first-run success.

---

## 1. Workflow Architecture — Two Files

Use **two separate workflow files** to avoid duplicate runs on PRs.

| File | Trigger | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `pr-check.yml` | `pull_request` targeting `main`, `develop` | Lint + test + build + Sonar PR gate |
| `deploy.yml` | `push` to `main`, `develop` | Lint + test + build + Sonar branch tracking + deploy |

---

## 2. SonarCloud Configuration

### Install sonar-scanner

Use the `sonar-scanner` CLI (JavaScript/TypeScript scanner):

```bash
npm install -D sonar-scanner
```

Or use the GitHub Action:

```yaml
- name: SonarCloud Scan
  uses: SonarSource/sonarcloud-github-action@v2
  env:
    SONAR_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.SONAR_TOKEN }}
```

### sonar-project.properties

Create `sonar-project.properties` at the workspace root:

```properties
sonar.projectKey=your-project-key
sonar.organization=your-org
sonar.sources=apps/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/src
sonar.tests=apps/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/src
sonar.test.inclusions=**/*.spec.ts
sonar.exclusions=**/node_modules/**,**/dist/**,**/*.spec.ts
sonar.typescript.lcov.reportPaths=coverage/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/lcov.info
sonar.coverage.exclusions=**/*.spec.ts,**/environments/**
```

---

## 3. Coverage Reporting

Jest produces lcov coverage reports. Configure in `jest.config.ts` or via CLI:

```bash
npx nx test {{ model.manifest.service_name }} --coverage --coverageReporters=lcov
```

The lcov report is written to `coverage/{{ model.manifest.service_name }}/lcov.info`.

Pass this path to SonarCloud via `sonar.typescript.lcov.reportPaths`.

---

## 4. PR Analysis

For PR-based analysis, the SonarCloud GitHub Action automatically detects PR context. No additional parameters needed when using the official action.

If using the CLI directly:

```bash
sonar-scanner \
  -Dsonar.pullrequest.key=$PR_NUMBER \
  -Dsonar.pullrequest.branch=$HEAD_BRANCH \
  -Dsonar.pullrequest.base=$BASE_BRANCH
```

---

## 5. Quality Gate Strategy

| Workflow | Gate Behavior | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| `deploy.yml` | Track only (no block) | Dashboard health tracking |
| `pr-check.yml` | Block on failure | Enforce quality on new code |

The 80% coverage condition applies to **new code lines in the PR only**, not overall coverage.

---

## 6. Required Exclusions

Always exclude test files and generated output from coverage analysis:

```properties
sonar.exclusions=**/node_modules/**,**/dist/**,**/*.spec.ts
sonar.coverage.exclusions=**/*.spec.ts,**/environments/**,**/test-setup.ts
```

---

## 7. Setup Checklist

```
[ ] Create SonarCloud project — note the project key and org slug
[ ] Add SONAR_TOKEN as a GitHub Actions secret
[ ] Create sonar-project.properties with lcov report path
[ ] Add SonarCloud scan step to pr-check.yml and deploy.yml
[ ] Run first analysis on main to seed the baseline
[ ] Verify PR analysis shows new code coverage
[ ] Enable quality gate enforcement on pr-check.yml
```
